# TTP-2026-0165 — Microsoft SharePoint & OneDrive Enumeration (SIM-CLOUD-009)
# XQL paste-buffer generated by detection_scanner/scripts/export_artifacts.py

## ABIOC — Microsoft SharePoint enumeration activity (behavioral-ML, causality-anchored)
# severity: medium
# behavioral_profile: machine-learning
# causality_anchor: Learned per-identity SharePoint access baseline (typical search/page volume and distinct search-term breadth per session); the alert anchors the burst to the same UserId + ClientIP that broke that baseline.
# ML analytic (is_ml=true) that baselines each identity's normal SharePoint access breadth and velocity and raises an alert when one UserId/ClientIP performs an unusually large burst of search/page operations spanning many distinct search terms across a site in a short window — the cloud-service-discovery shape of repository enumeration ahead of collection.

dataset = msft_o365_audit
| filter Workload = "SharePoint"
| filter Operation in ("SearchQueryPerformed", "PageViewed")
| comp count() as page_events, count_distinct(SearchQueryText) as distinct_searches by UserId, ClientIP
| filter page_events >= 20 and distinct_searches >= 5
| fields UserId, ClientIP, page_events, distinct_searches

## ABIOC — Microsoft OneDrive enumeration activity (behavioral-ML, causality-anchored)
# severity: medium
# behavioral_profile: machine-learning
# causality_anchor: Learned per-identity OneDrive file-access baseline (typical distinct files touched per session); the alert anchors the enumeration burst to the same UserId + ClientIP that deviated from it.
# ML analytic (is_ml=true) that baselines each identity's normal OneDrive for Business file-access breadth and raises an alert when one UserId/ClientIP rapidly enumerates an unusually large, distinct set of files (FileAccessed / FileDownloaded sweep) — cloud-service discovery of the repository ahead of bulk collection.

dataset = msft_o365_audit
| filter Workload = "OneDrive"
| filter Operation in ("FileAccessed", "FileDownloaded", "FileSyncDownloadedFull")
| comp count() as file_events, count_distinct(ObjectId) as distinct_files by UserId, ClientIP
| filter file_events >= 25 and distinct_files >= 8
| fields UserId, ClientIP, file_events, distinct_files

## VALIDATION — Microsoft 365 audit enumeration landing validation
# purpose: validation
# dataset: msft_o365_audit

dataset = msft_o365_audit
| filter _time > to_timestamp(current_time() - 900)
| filter Workload in ("SharePoint", "OneDrive")
| filter Operation in ("SearchQueryPerformed", "PageViewed", "FileAccessed", "FileDownloaded", "FileSyncDownloadedFull")
| comp count() as observed_events, count_distinct(ObjectId) as distinct_objects by UserId, ClientIP, Workload
| filter observed_events >= 1
| fields UserId, ClientIP, Workload, observed_events, distinct_objects

